non-commercial research, teaching and study, including within academic
institutions. Any work resulting from its use must cite the SCAFFL project
(see CITATION.cff). Without prior written permission you may NOT use it
commercially (including selling it or offering it as a paid service) and you
may NOT distribute, publish, redistribute or sublicense copies, in whole or in
part, original or modified. Forks within GitHub are allowed only as required by
GitHub's Terms of Service, for contributing to this project. Contributions are
licensed to the copyright holder. Provided "AS IS", without warranty.
